      "source": {
        "profile": "band-contract/file-source/1",
        "format": "frontmatter",
        "content": "---\nname: explicit-infinity\ndescription: Test explicit infinity with explicit roles and outcomes.\nengine: 0.2.0-lab.1\nroles: [a, b]\n---\n\"\"\"\nA keeps a connection to B alive with pings for as long as needed, then closes it. There is no\ntime limit.\n\"\"\"\ncontract @infinity mentions 1 => expired\n\n\"\"\"\nYou are A. Ping B while the connection is in use, and close it when you are done.\n\"\"\"\nrole a\n\n\"\"\"\nYou are B. Receive A's pings and close; you send nothing in this session.\n\"\"\"\nrole b\n\n\"\"\"\nSignal that the connection is still in use. The message carries no content.\n\"\"\"\ntype ping\n  text: text(bytes: 4, graphemes: 1)\n\n\"\"\"\nClose the connection. No pings follow.\n\"\"\"\ntype close\n\n\"\"\"\nThe connection is open. A may ping any number of times and closes it when done.\n\"\"\"\nstate new\n  event a -> b: ping()\n  a -> b: close() => complete\n\n\"\"\"\nA closed the connection. Send nothing more.\n\"\"\"\nend complete\n\n\"\"\"\nThe session expired. Send nothing more.\n\"\"\"\nend expired\n",
        "sha256": "90c83a6650222fbdf2b19207e5f94fa3ade56feeee6bcb32e8343567749f7024"
      }
    },
